  "error_map": {
    "401:authError": "auth_expired",
    "401:required": "auth_expired",
    "403:forbidden": "permission_denied",
    "403:insufficientPermissions": "permission_denied",
    "403:accessNotConfigured": "permission_denied",
    "403:dailyLimitExceeded": "provider_transient",
    "403:quotaExceeded": "provider_transient",
    "403:rateLimitExceeded": "provider_transient",
    "403:userRateLimitExceeded": "provider_transient",
    "400:badRequest": "invalid_request",
    "400:invalid": "invalid_request",
    "400:invalidParameter": "invalid_request",
    "404:notFound": "invalid_request",
    "500:internalError": "provider_transient",
    "503:backendError": "provider_transient"
  },
  "_error_map_note": "Codes are the reason strings of the standard Google API Console error envelope, which the Search Console API v1 (https://developers.google.com/webmaster-tools/v1/errors, endpoint https://developers.google.com/webmaster-tools/v1/searchanalytics/query) returns unchanged. SHAPE THE KEYS MATCH: { error: { code: <numeric http>, message, errors: [{ message, domain, reason: '<reason>' }] } }. core.pull_errors._extract_provider_codes yields errors[].reason before error.status and error.code, so every key here is written on errors[].reason. error.code is deliberately never keyed on -- it repeats the HTTP status and could only produce '401:401', which refines nothing (that was the reason this map stood empty until 2026-08-17). WHAT THE MAP CHANGES vs the pure-HTTP classification: the four 403 quota reasons (dailyLimitExceeded / quotaExceeded / rateLimitExceeded / userRateLimitExceeded) become provider_transient instead of permission_denied -- Google documents them as 'retry using exponential backoff', while permission_denied is retryable=False and told the operator to reconnect a credential that was never the problem; 404 notFound becomes invalid_request instead of unclassified, so a siteUrl that no longer resolves stops being replayed. No 429 key: HTTP 429 raises core.quota.RateLimitError in the connector (breaker path) and never reaches classify_http_error. No auth_revoked entry: Search Console answers a revoked grant with the same 401 authError as an expired token, so there is no code to key one on.",
  "account_topology": {
    "_comment": "Story 25.7 (AC4): GSC topology is a single flat level \u2014 the token's reachable sites (GSC properties). The reporting entity (selection_level) is the SITE (a searchanalytics.query call targets sites/{siteUrl}/searchAnalytics/query). discover_accounts calls the Webmasters API sites.list endpoint to enumerate what the token can access. Core owns selection/access-check/trial/backfill. Replaces the GSC_SITE_URL env-var pattern (removed 2026-07-31; see ROLLOUT_NOTES.md \u2014 _resolve_site_url now raises when no site was selected, an env-var being one property for the whole deployment).",
    "levels": [
      {
        "id": "site",
        "label": "Site (GSC property)"
      }
    ],
    "selection_level": "site",
    "discovery": {
      "callable": "discover_accounts"
    },
    "pull_parameter": "site_url"
  },
  "quota": {
    "window_seconds": 100,
    "budget_points": 1200,
    "read_cost": 1,
    "write_cost": 1
  },
